artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $F$ be a field and let $H = C_3 \times C_3$ be embedded as a transitive subgroup of the symmetric group $S_9$ via its regular representation (so that $H$ acts on the set $\{1,2,\dots,9\}$ by left multiplication after a fixed identification of this set with the underlying set of $H$). Let $H$ act on the rational function field $F(x_1,\dots,x_9)$ by permuting the variables according to this embedding $H \hookrightarrow S_9$, and define
$$Z_H(F,9) := F(x_1,\dots,x_9)^{H}.$$
Determine whether the field $Z_H(F,9)$ is:
(a) rational (i.e., purely transcendental) over $F$;
(b) stably rational over $F$ (i.e., $Z_H(F,9)(y_1,\dots,y_m)$ is purely transcendental over $F$ for some $m\ge 0$);
(c) retract rational over $F$ (in the sense of Saltman: $Z_H(F,9)$ is the fraction field of an $F$-algebra $A$ such that the identity map of $A$ factors through a localization of a polynomial $F$-algebra).

